hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16016","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said, Hilal ibn Amir al-Muzani narrated to us, from his father, he said, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressing the people at Mina upon a mule, and upon him was a red cloak, he said, and a man of the people of Badr was before him conveying from him, he said, so I came until I put my hand between his foot and his sandal strap, he said, and I kept marveling at its coolness."
"16017","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said, a shaykh of Banu Fazarah narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Amir al-Muzani, from his father, he said, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressing the people upon a gray mule, and Ali was conveying from him."
